  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 111 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThursday into Thursday night...the upper ridge will remain centered \nover the Four Corners Region into the Southern Plains. This will \nbring a continued northwest flow aloft across the Northern and \nCentral Plains. An H7 trough axis will move eastward across north \ncentral and central NE Thursday morning. This will aid in bringing \nchance to likely POPs to these areas, with likely POPs east of \nBroken Bow through Bassett. Meanwhile, an H7 closed low over \nsouthwest SD will drop southeast across north central NE into \neastern NE during the afternoon and evening. This will bring chance \nPOPs across the area, especially during the evening. NBM 24hr hour \nprobabilities for greater than 0.10 inch is from 40 to 75 percent \neast of Highway 83. \n\nThe upper ridge is forecast to build northward into the region \nFriday through Sunday. Mainly dry conditions, although isolated \nthunderstorms are possible. H7 temperatures around 15C Friday warm \nto 17 to around 20C Saturday through Monday. Mainly dry conditions, \nalthough isolated storms appear possible during the late afternoon \nhours Saturday and Sunday, despite the warm temperatures aloft. \n\nHighs Thursday from the upper 70s east, where clouds and \nprecipitation are expected, to the upper 80s far southwest. \n\nFriday should see highs slightly above normal in the west to \nslightly below normal east (low to mid 90s west, and mid 80s east). \nHot temperatures are likely to return Saturday through Monday. Upper \n90s to around 100 Saturday and Sunday and mid to upper 90s\nMonday.",
